Rule 1 (input tensor must be at least 1-dimensional)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 2 (output tensor should have same number of dimensions as input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 3 (input tensor must contain non-zero elements)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∃i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : v_1[i] ≠ 0
>>
Rule 8 (input tensor must have compatible shape for argwhere)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) = 1 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 12 (input tensor must have same shape as output tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) ≠ 0 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 18 (input tensor must be 1-dimensional)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 1
